From: Ray Liu <ray.xy.liu@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 14 May 2026 09:22:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] net: airoha: AN7563 debug - log RX SPORT decoding (TEMP)

Even with NPU node + GPL firmware in place (commit 940ec67ce5) and
FW_LOADER_USER_HELPER disabled so request_firmware() short-circuits
to -EPROBE_DEFER until rootfs mount (commit 35e45e9bc2), Windows ping
to / from AN7563 still hits 100% loss with no AN7563 RX trace ever
firing in airoha_qdma_rx_process().

Likely root cause: AN7563 silicon fills the FE QDMA RX descriptor
SPORT field (QDMA_ETH_RXMSG_SPORT_MASK) with a value outside the
EN7581 ranges (0x18, 0x16, 0x10..0x14, 0x2..0x4) that
airoha_qdma_get_gdm_port() recognises, so every RX descriptor returns
-EINVAL and lands at free_frag long before the existing
dev_info_ratelimited() in the DSA branch.

Add temporary dev_info_ratelimited() traces inside
airoha_qdma_get_gdm_port() (both success and EINVAL paths) and at the
free_frag goto in airoha_qdma_rx_process() so we can see in dmesg
exactly what SPORT value the silicon fills and whether the packet is
being dropped because of an unknown SPORT or because eth->ports[p]
is NULL.

Debug only - drop or fold into a permanent AN7563 SPORT mapping fix
once the value is known.

Signed-off-by: Ray Liu <ray.xy.liu@gmail.com>
---
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.c
@@ -629,9 +629,16 @@
 		port = sport - 1;
 		break;
 	default:
+		dev_info_ratelimited(eth->dev,
+			"AN7563 RX: get_gdm_port EINVAL sport=0x%x msg1=0x%08x\n",
+			sport, msg1);
 		return -EINVAL;
 	}
 
+	dev_info_ratelimited(eth->dev,
+		"AN7563 RX: get_gdm_port sport=0x%x -> port=%u (eth->ports[port]=%s)\n",
+		sport, port, eth->ports[port] ? "valid" : "NULL");
+
 	return port >= ARRAY_SIZE(eth->ports) ? -EINVAL : port;
 }
 
@@ -671,8 +678,13 @@
 			goto free_frag;
 
 		p = airoha_qdma_get_gdm_port(eth, desc);
-		if (p < 0 || !eth->ports[p])
+		if (p < 0 || !eth->ports[p]) {
+			dev_info_ratelimited(eth->dev,
+				"AN7563 RX: free_frag p=%d eth->ports[p]=%s\n",
+				p,
+				(p >= 0 && p < (int)ARRAY_SIZE(eth->ports) && eth->ports[p]) ? "valid" : "NULL");
 			goto free_frag;
+		}
 
 		port = eth->ports[p];
 		if (!q->skb) { /* first buffer */
